      "updated_at": "2026-07-03T13:16:07Z",
      "body": "> I can implement my own context manager or refactor my code to make it work again.\n> \n> Is there a valid use case to use an already finalized recording with a context manager? If not, could you throw an exception in this case?\n\nYa the short term work around would be to just call into `rerun.set_global_data_recording` or `rerun.set_thread_local_data_recording` directly to maintain the previous behavior.\n\nI think we'll need to think about this a bit more next week. Potentially throwing the exception, or potentially restructuring this a bit to make things clearer.\n",
